  (text "Notes\nJ1: Long header: RST end at the USB-C edge\nR4: The latch: VOUT holds ON where GPIO 17 left it\nC2: CT to VIN: about 4 ms turn-on\nJ4: Waveshare HAT order: VCC GND DIN CLK CS DC RST BUSY PWR\nJ5: For the HAT's Dupont lead\nJ3: 1 GND (key and LED), 2 key, 3 LED +\nR1: Pull-up\nSW1: In parallel with the off-board key\nJ14: 1 EN (Pi gpio_en), 2 BOOT (Pi gpio_boot), 3 GND\nD3: Cathode at the bench\nD4: Cathode at the bench\nR10: Holds RST at 3.0 V against the Pi pull-down\nR11: GPIO 0 stays high unless the bench pulls it\nJ7: Qwiic: RV-8803\nJ8: Qwiic: Notecarrier-X, its 3.3 V open\nJP1: Open: the Notecarrier's 3.3 V stays unconnected (§33.2)\nJ9: From the Feather's I2C2 STEMMA QT\nJ12: §40.2 analog board: enable GPIO 18, isolator side 1 on I2C2\nJ13: §40.2 serial port: enable GPIO 33, RX GPIO 14\nJ15: Free header pins" (at 20 225 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid d41f05b2-9a34-5ecf-a780-7254091de65c))
